{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1477335-aberrant-tell-me-the-deal-with-the-rules-revisions","id":1477335,"title":"[Aberrant] Tell me the deal with the rules revisions.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-03-25T09:08:24-07:00","id":1477335,"title":"[Aberrant] Tell me the deal with the rules revisions.","content":"Hey, all!<br /> I came onto the forums looking to see if people are having the same kind of issues with the Trinity Continuum rules as I have been and was looking for clarification. While I'm much more confident with the rules after reading what stuff y'all have been talking about, I did notice one thing keep popping up from time to time:<br /> <br /> The devs are currently not taking rules questions for Aberrant because they are revising the rules currently.<br /> <br /> Is this true?<br /> What is the major source of the rule confusion exactly? I feel like perhaps it has to do with some unclear wording on a few pages here and there, but is it deeper than that? Please bring me up to speed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1468-blindeye","name":"Blindeye","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1468_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-25T10:17:49-07:00","id":1477342,"title":"","content":"Not any more. They were revising in the period between the end of the KS and the release of the final PDF (sometime last year, or so).<br /> <br /> As I see there is no major rules questions, other than small issues with people expecting rules to work a certain way and getting frustrated (injuries and specialities mainly). If the group is not used to the way momentum work (shared pool that refills by fails) it can keep the group from operations at full power. Helping each other in the actions and spending successes can also take time to work with a more traditional table, as the rules follow a more narrative approach than the old system.<br /> <br /> Intrigue and Investigation, due to the amount of power given to the players, requires an imaginative GM, at least good at improvisation, but this kind of power can be discussed with the players\u2026 not big deal.<br /> <br /> There are some issues that require attention when dealing with Super Science, that comes from Core and were taken to another level due to the importance of Nova and Q tech, but it\u2019s not THAT big if you find where the lose ends in the rules are and set the way it must work.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-25T11:47:47-07:00","id":1477346,"title":"","content":"<br /> Well, Mr.Luz I have to say I agree with almost all your posts about the rules. If there's not forthcoming explanations then I just wanted to bring up one thing that makes sense to me, but gets argued about on here. Does this jive with your understanding of the rules:<br /> <br /> I think a really big misunderstanding is with Scale on attack rolls. This bit of figuring out is what brought me here originally. I see a few people point to the core rules, except that Scale is explicitly re-contextualized into six categories, none of which has (as you've put it) &quot;Precision Scale&quot;. I think as intended, the only Enhancement to attack rolls is from the weapon, which generally is from +1 to +3, and with Defensive actions, it seems equally hard to get *any* Scale applied. I imagine there's a lot of players who apply Mega-Might Scale to all Close Range attacks and Mega-Dex (which specifically doesn't apply Scale to anything out of the box) to Aim attack, but this is not as intended.<br /> <br /> Do you think I've got this figured out? I mainly realized I had to throw out assumptions I was making from Aberrant 1e and certain editions of Scion. On top of that, I tried to write my own Superhero TRPG pre-Aberrant 2e and came to a lot of similar conclusions that you need to keep a tight cap on min-maxing in superhero games.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1468-blindeye","name":"Blindeye","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1468_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-25T14:39:39-07:00","id":1477363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blindeye</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1477335-aberrant-tell-me-the-deal-with-the-rules-revisions#post1477335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The devs are currently not taking rules questions for Aberrant because they are revising the rules currently.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was the period between then the backer PDF went out -- and we were revising the book based on feedback -- and the final release of the book. That was June of last year, which is almost a year ago now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-25T20:22:36-07:00","id":1477389,"title":"","content":"Well, Mega-Might only applies to the damage itself and not to the attack. You can buy Inflict Damage multiple times based on Scale difference. It is not meant as Enhancement to the roll itself.<br /> Mega-Dex makes it easier to hit someone if you want to use Dex on a roll.<br /> But the combat itself balances out since there is Defense score that you still have to overcome to land that hit. However, if a Mega-Might character lands that hit? Then the lower Scaled Durability character is going to be pasted.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-25T20:57:47-07:00","id":1477401,"title":"","content":"Kind of, yes. Scale is incredibly forgiving of being on the short end, if you're a significant character (which the player characters are by definition). So getting hit by someone with more Might Scale than you will definitely <i>hurt</i> more; but it's not going to be a death blow. On the other hand, if an extra gets hit and has the same deficit of Might Scale, he's going to be pasted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-25T21:43:10-07:00","id":1477404,"title":"","content":"&quot;pasted&quot; was just a dramatic turn of phrase.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":786,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","user":"thedonnie","date":". 03-26-2022, 12:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-26T03:52:31-07:00","id":1477430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1477335-aberrant-tell-me-the-deal-with-the-rules-revisions?p=1477342#post1477342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I see there is no major rules questions, other than small issues with people expecting rules to work a certain way and getting frustrated (injuries and specialities mainly).</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, there are also legit issues with the rules that don't get addressed either (see the recent commentary about Digital Manipulation dots) or, sometimes when addressed contradict the rules as written (for example, Power Scale explicitly listing guns as Scale 2 but dev intent is that guns are Power Scale 1).<br /> <br /> There are issues as you describe too, for sure, but let's not put it all on people &quot;expecting rules to work a certain way&quot; when there is more than just that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26905-eternl-knight","name":"Eternl Knight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26905_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-26T05:17:35-07:00","id":1477434,"title":"","content":"<b>On the issue of Scale vs Enhancement in Combat:</b><br /> <br /> It seems you have it mostly right as I understand it. I think the reason for there being no &quot;Precision Scale&quot; (and it's counter &quot;Dodge Scale&quot;) is because it makes Mega-Dexterity the &quot;God stat&quot; (which is something pretty much every super-hero game suffers from). Better to simply make it an Enhancement only thing and allow some chance of hitting The Flash than make all speedsters impossible to touch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26905-eternl-knight","name":"Eternl Knight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26905_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-26T11:03:40-07:00","id":1477455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eternl Knight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1477335-aberrant-tell-me-the-deal-with-the-rules-revisions?p=1477434#post1477434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>On the issue of Scale vs Enhancement in Combat:</b><br /> <br /> It seems you have it mostly right as I understand it. I think the reason for there being no &amp;quot;Precision Scale&amp;quot; (and it's counter &amp;quot;Dodge Scale&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> is because it makes Mega-Dexterity the &amp;quot;God stat&amp;quot; (which is something pretty much every super-hero game suffers from). Better to simply make it an Enhancement only thing and allow some chance of hitting The Flash than make all speedsters impossible to touch.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. I never thought of this being a problem, but I guess that\u2019s cause I haven\u2019t played that many superhero games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-26T14:11:35-07:00","id":1477476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blindeye</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1477335-aberrant-tell-me-the-deal-with-the-rules-revisions?p=1477346#post1477346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think I've got this figured out? I mainly realized I had to throw out assumptions I was making from Aberrant 1e and certain editions of Scion. On top of that, I tried to write my own Superhero TRPG pre-Aberrant 2e and came to a lot of similar conclusions that you need to keep a tight cap on min-maxing in superhero games.</div> </div> </div> </div>You got what I meant. Aberrant 1e and Scion 1e were amazing games and I had a lot of fun playing, but there were some fails in their conception that I like to think were solved in TC Aberrant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eternl Knight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1477335-aberrant-tell-me-the-deal-with-the-rules-revisions?p=1477430#post1477430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, there are also legit issues with the rules that don't get addressed either (see the recent commentary about Digital Manipulation dots) or, sometimes when addressed contradict the rules as written (for example, Power Scale explicitly listing guns as Scale 2 but dev intent is that guns are Power Scale 1).</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant general issues, not specific issues. Aberrant 1e had a issue with the big piles of dice and the need of certain builds to become functional in the game, that\u2019s structural as I see. The workings of a power or the content of a table are specific issues as I see. I agree there are a bunch of small issues, but in the very end they are solvable with a simple discussion at the table. Structural changes needs houserules and play tests to make it work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-29T19:16:39-07:00","id":1477661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1477335-aberrant-tell-me-the-deal-with-the-rules-revisions?p=1477476#post1477476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I meant general issues, not specific issues.</div> </div> </div> </div>This I'll grant you. TC:Aberrant is <i><b>much</b></i> better structurally than Aberrant 1e. It is more limited, mathematically &amp; in power concepts, but those limitations bring about as much balance as one can get from a super-heroes game without going full Hero/Champions crunchy (&amp; even then, it has some issues). The concept of Scale helps a lot too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1477335-aberrant-tell-me-the-deal-with-the-rules-revisions?p=1477476#post1477476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree there are a bunch of small issues, but in the very end they are solvable with a simple discussion at the table. Structural changes needs houserules and play tests to make it work.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, the &quot;small issues&quot; (as you see them) need house-rules and play tests to make work too. The &quot;simple discussion at the table&quot; is the starting point, but some of those small issues flow into other ones.<br /> <br /> Take, for example, the <i>&quot;Guns are Scale 2 according to one part of the book but treated (though not stated) as Scale 1 in other parts&quot;</i>. Make pistols Scale 1 by default, and they're no better than knives. Same range, same enhancement, same skill-set to hit a target shooting/thrown, etc. Which makes <b>no</b> sense, so you discuss it and make them Scale 2. Then in play-testing, you find you need to give Scale 2 to flak jacket armour, etc. Ask me how I know. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26905-eternl-knight","name":"Eternl Knight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26905_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}